  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R1 and R2 establish that moment tensor potentials can model a closely related BCC refractory high-entropy alloy and that short-range order can materially affect its behavior. R3 and R15 independently reinforce SRO as a consequential structural feature in BCC refractory HEAs, while R5 shows that finite-temperature electronic contributions can alter alloy phase stability. R4 supplies the exact W-Ta-V-Cr alloy family but not the computational method. However, none of the records proposes training a liquid-phase MTP to reproduce the DFT phase-space distribution, replacing thermodynamic integration with MTP-to-DFT free-energy perturbation, or using the small energy-difference variance to accelerate melting free-energy calculations. The records therefore point toward relevant ingredients but leave the central FEP-based intervention and its integration into a melting-point workflow as a substantial new idea."
